<% layout('./layout') %>
<% const s = it.settings %>
<form class="card narrow"
      data-signals="<%= JSON.stringify({ originZip: s.origin_zip, uspsZone: String(s.usps_zone), upsZone: String(s.ups_zone), upsDimDivisor: String(s.ups_dim_divisor), taxPct: String(s.tax_pct), uspsDiscountPct: String(s.usps_discount_pct), categoryId: s.category_id }) %>"
      data-on:submit__prevent="@post('/settings')"
      data-indicator="_busy">
  <h1>Settings</h1>

  <fieldset>
    <legend>Ship from</legend>
    <div class="field-grid">
      <label class="field">
        <span>Your ZIP (where you ship from)</span>
        <input type="text" inputmode="numeric" pattern="\d{5}" maxlength="5" autocomplete="postal-code" data-bind="originZip">
      </label>
      <div class="field align-end">
        <button type="button" class="secondary" data-on:click="@post('/settings/zone')" data-attr:disabled="$_busy || $originZip.length !== 5">Find furthest zone</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="hint">Zones measure distance from this ZIP: zone 1 is nearby, zone 8 is the far side of the country. This looks up the official USPS zone chart for your ZIP and picks the furthest zone in the lower 48 (no AK, HI, territories or military).<% if (s.zone_checked_at) { %> Last checked against the chart effective <%= s.zone_checked_at %>.<% } %></p>
    <div class="field-grid">
      <label class="field">
        <span>Worst USPS zone</span>
        <input type="number" min="1" max="8" step="1" data-bind="uspsZone">
      </label>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Worst UPS Ground zone</span>
        <input type="number" min="2" max="8" step="1" data-bind="upsZone">
      </label>
    </div>
    <label class="field">
      <span>eBay Labels discount on USPS</span>
      <span class="affix" data-suffix="%"><input type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" max="90" step="0.1" data-bind="uspsDiscountPct"></span>
    </label>
    <p class="hint">Taken off the USPS Commercial rates in Rates to match what eBay charges you for a label. Compare an eBay label quote with the same cell in Rates to find it. Cells you've edited are used as-is.</p>
    <p class="hint">UPS zones differ from USPS zones. Check yours on UPS's zone chart for your ZIP, under "Calculate time and cost" → zone charts.</p>
  </fieldset>

  <fieldset>
    <legend>Defaults</legend>
    <div class="field-grid">
      <label class="field">
        <span>Average buyer sales tax</span>
        <span class="affix" data-suffix="%"><input type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" max="20" step="0.01" data-bind="taxPct"></span>
      </label>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Default category</span>
        <select data-bind="categoryId">
<% for (const c of it.categories) { %>
          <option value="<%= c.id %>"><%= c.name %></option>
<% } %>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label class="field">
        <span>UPS dim divisor</span>
        <input type="number" min="100" max="400" step="1" data-bind="upsDimDivisor">
      </label>
    </div>
    <p class="hint">eBay charges its final value fee on the sales tax as well, so a higher tax rate raises your fees. The US average combined rate is about 7–8%. UPS dimensional weight is L×W×H ÷ divisor (139 is standard).</p>
  </fieldset>

  <fieldset>
    <legend>Chrome extension</legend>
    <p>Copies weight, box size, ship-to ZIP and the USPS Ground Advantage price from eBay's shipping calculator into this calculator.</p>
    <p><a href="/extension.zip" download>Download the extension (.zip)</a></p>
    <ol class="hint">
      <li>Unzip it. You get a <code>ship-pad-extension</code> folder.</li>
      <li>Open <code>chrome://extensions</code> and turn on <strong>Developer mode</strong>.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Load unpacked</strong> and pick that folder, then pin it from the puzzle-piece menu.</li>
      <li>Open Ship Pad's calculator once, then click <strong>Open eBay calculator</strong>. On eBay, click the extension's icon: Ship Pad opens in Chrome's side panel. Its "From eBay" box updates as you type on eBay, and after you click Calculate, clicking into the panel fills everything in.</li>
    </ol>
  </fieldset>

  <div class="actions">
    <button type="submit" data-attr:disabled="$_busy">Save settings</button>
    <p id="settings-status" class="status" role="status"></p>
  </div>
</form>
